{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-016", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indian central bank keeps repo rate unchanged at 5.25%", "content": "Downside risks to growth and upside risks to inflation prompted India’s central bank to keep the policy repo rate on hold at 5.25 per cent. \nWith this, the bank has been on hold in three consecutive meetings this year. \nIt revised FY27 real GDP projection downward to 6.6 per cent from 6.9 per cent earlier and raised retail inflation projection for the fiscal to 5.1 per cent from 4.6 per cent earlier. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indian-central-bank-keeps-repo-rate-unchanged-at-5-25--310806-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-017", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.33, "keywords": ["improve", "loss", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Strong US export sales fail to halt ICE cotton slide", "content": "ICE cotton futures extended losses as falling crude oil prices and rising certified stocks outweighed strong US export sales.\nJuly settled at 74.89 cents/lb, down 1.84 cents, while October and December also fell sharply.\nCertified stocks reached their highest level since 2017.\nLower crude oil improved polyester’s competitiveness, adding pressure on cotton prices.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/strong-us-export-sales-fail-to-halt-ice-cotton-slide-310803-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-018", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s Tamil Nadu textile sector may save $340 mn via renewables", "content": "India’s Tamil Nadu textile industry could save up to ₹3,250 crore (~$340 million) annually by shifting to renewable electricity while reducing carbon emissions and improving competitiveness.\nRising fuel costs and growing global sustainability pressures are increasing production challenges, while clean energy adoption could also reduce dependence on biomass and lower environmental impact.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-tamil-nadu-textile-sector-may-save-340-mn-via-renewables-310800-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-019", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India waives cotton import duty. Will it actually change sourcing?", "content": "India’s temporary cotton import duty waiver may improve textile competitiveness amid China+1 sourcing shifts and upcoming FTAs with the UK, EU and New Zealand.\nIndustry leaders say awareness remains low and price benefits may take months to reach factories.\nLong-term growth still depends on stable cotton prices, quality, logistics and supply-chain efficiency.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-waives-cotton-import-duty-will-it-actually-change-sourcing--310798-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-020", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Brazil cotton prices climb for fourth month on tight selling", "content": "Brazil cotton prices rose for a fourth straight month in May as growers held remaining 2024-25 stocks and strong exports absorbed surplus supplies, according to CEPEA. \nThe CEPEA/ESALQ Index gained 3.31 per cent during the month. \nMeanwhile, ICAC lowered its 2026-27 global cotton output forecast and projected Brazil’s cotton area to fall 6 per cent, reducing production by 10 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/-brazil-cotton-prices-climb-for-fourth-month-on-tight-selling--310796-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-021", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.17, "keywords": ["growth", "expand", "uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "How Vietnam became an FTA success story", "content": "FTAs have shifted from diplomatic tools to strategic drivers of competitiveness and growth by expanding market access, cutting tariffs and stabilising trade rules amid global uncertainty. \nVietnam stands out for embedding FTAs into its economic strategy, using agreements like CPTPP, EVFTA and RCEP to deepen global trade links, attract investment and fuel strong export-led manufacturing growth.  ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/how-vietnam-became-an-fta-success-story-310786-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lululemon-2026-06-05-022", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lululemon"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["growth", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Canada’s Lululemon reports mixed Q1 results, lowers FY26 outlook", "content": "Lululemon has reported mixed Q1 FY26 results, with net revenue rising 4 per cent to $2.5 billion, driven by 22 per cent international growth, while Americas revenue declined 3 per cent. \nGross margin fell 410 basis points to 54.2 per cent and diluted EPS dropped to $1.69. \nThe company lowered its FY26 outlook, citing macroeconomic headwinds and softer demand in the Americas market. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/canada-s-lululemon-reports-mixed-q1-results-lowers-fy26-outlook-310802-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-023", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "improve", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US’ Caleres reports strong Q1 FY26 growth led by Brand Portfolio", "content": "Caleres has reported Q1 FY26 net sales of $666.6 million, up 8.5 per cent YoY, driven by 20.6 per cent growth in its Brand Portfolio business. \nAdjusted EPS rose to $0.38, exceeding guidance, while gross margin improved 200 basis points to 47.3 per cent. \nFamous Footwear sales declined 2.5 per cent. \nThe company expects modest sales growth and improved profitability for full-year FY26. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-caleres-reports-strong-q1-fy26-growth-led-by-brand-portfolio-310799-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
